near algebra (version 5.0.1), \u003chttps://eigen.tuxfamily.org\u003e\n * GTest, Google\u0027s C++ testing framework (version 1.16.0), \u003chttps://github.com/google/googletest\u003e\n   Ceres unit tests\n\n-- The following RECOMMENDED packages have been found:\n\n * LAPACK, Linear Algebra PACKage implementation\n * SuiteSparse (required version \u003e\u003d 4.5.6), A suite of sparse matrix algorithms (version 7.12.2), \u003chttps://github.com/DrTimothyAldenDavis/SuiteSparse\u003e\n\n-- The following REQUIRED packages have been found:\n\n * Threads, Native platform threading support\n   Multithreading support\n\n-- The following features have been disabled:\n\n * CUDA acceleration, CUDA-accelerated linear solvers\n * cuDSS sparse solver, cuDSS sparse linear solver support\n * Documentation, Ceres HTML documentation\n * Eigen METIS, METIS ordering for Eigen sparse solvers\n * CHOLMOD Partition, CHOLMOD graph partitioning support\n * Shared library, Shared Ceres library\n\n-- The following OPTIONAL packages have not been found:\n\n * CUDAToolkit, NVIDIA CUDA toolkit, \u003chttps://developer.nvidia.com/cuda-toolkit\u003e\n   CUDA solver acceleration\n * cudss, NVIDIA CUDA sparse solver library, \u003chttps://developer.nvidia.com/cudss\u003e\n   CUDA sparse solver support\n * OpenMP, OpenMP parallel execution API\n   Parallel execution support\n * TBB, Threading Building Blocks\n   SuiteSparseQR dependency\n\n-- The following RECOMMENDED packages have not been found:\n\n * METIS, Serial graph partitioning and fill-reducing matrix ordering\n\n-- Configuring done (15.6s)\n-- Generating done (1.1s)\n-- Build files have been written to: /Users/sameeragarwal/ceres-solver/cmake-build",
